1
00:00:10,025 --> 00:00:16,290
On Friday, 22 November 1963, the President of the United States landed in Dallas,

2
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,127
Texas, where a crowd was waiting.

3
00:00:18,597 --> 00:00:23,145
John F. Kennedy was forty-six years old, in the third year of his presidency.

4
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:26,430
In the Second World War he had commanded a navy boat,

5
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,887
PT 109, which a Japanese destroyer sank in 1943.

6
00:00:31,338 --> 00:00:35,243
In 1960 he won the White House by a very narrow margin,

7
00:00:35,293 --> 00:00:37,917
and became the youngest man ever elected president.

8
00:00:45,992 --> 00:00:50,957
In June 1963 he stood in West Berlin, in front of a vast crowd,

9
00:00:51,007 --> 00:00:53,602
and told them he too was a Berliner.

10
00:01:02,097 --> 00:01:08,097
But he had carried Texas in 1960 by a narrow margin, and for 1964 he needed it again,

11
00:01:08,147 --> 00:01:12,546
so in November 1963 he set out on a two-day trip across the state.

12
00:01:13,025 --> 00:01:16,170
This is the story of that trip, of the day it ended,

13
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:19,062
and of what the official record can and cannot tell us.

14
00:01:25,125 --> 00:01:27,881
The trip had two purposes, and neither was a secret.

15
00:01:28,358 --> 00:01:29,683
The first was votes,

16
00:01:29,733 --> 00:01:34,197
because the election was a year away and Texas was a large prize.

17
00:01:34,658 --> 00:01:37,283
The second was a quarrel inside his own party,

18
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:41,068
between Governor John Connally and Senator Ralph Yarborough.

19
00:01:41,558 --> 00:01:44,763
The schedule began on Thursday, 21 November,

20
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:48,201
with stops in San Antonio and Houston, and a night in Fort Worth.

21
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:50,206
A year earlier, in Houston,

22
00:01:50,206 --> 00:01:54,141
he had spoken at Rice University about sending Americans to the moon.

23
00:02:02,767 --> 00:02:05,366
An Air Force film of his visit to Cape Canaveral,

24
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:08,866
one week before Dallas, follows him on a tour of the space centre.

25
00:02:17,758 --> 00:02:21,423
On Friday morning in Fort Worth the weather was grey and wet,

26
00:02:21,473 --> 00:02:24,649
and at 8:45 he spoke to a crowd in the hotel parking lot.

27
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:29,690
At a breakfast, he joked that Mrs Kennedy takes longer to get ready than the men do,

28
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:30,628
but looks better.

29
00:02:31,097 --> 00:02:34,257
At 11:25 Air Force One took off for Dallas,

30
00:02:34,307 --> 00:02:36,052
a flight of about thirteen minutes.

31
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:40,409
The plan was a motorcade through the city and a luncheon at the Trade Mart.

32
00:02:46,492 --> 00:02:50,617
Air Force One touched down at Love Field at about 11:40 in the morning,

33
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:51,441
Dallas time.

34
00:03:07,725 --> 00:03:09,430
A crowd waited at the fence,

35
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,962
and the president and Mrs Kennedy walked along it, shaking hands.

36
00:03:13,425 --> 00:03:16,770
Not everyone in Dallas was friendly: that morning,

37
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:22,251
a black-bordered advertisement in the Dallas Morning News accused the president of favouring the nation's enemies.

38
00:03:22,725 --> 00:03:26,992
The president rode in an open limousine, with Governor Connally and his wife.

39
00:03:27,423 --> 00:03:32,082
The car had a clear plastic roof, but the sky had cleared, so it was left off.

40
00:03:32,558 --> 00:03:35,303
The motorcade left Love Field shortly before noon,

41
00:03:35,353 --> 00:03:38,207
and the route had been printed in the newspapers days before.

42
00:03:38,692 --> 00:03:42,037
It ran along Main Street, turned right onto Houston Street,

43
00:03:42,087 --> 00:03:43,578
and then left onto Elm Street.

44
00:03:44,063 --> 00:03:47,763
That turn took the cars past the Texas School Book Depository,

45
00:03:47,813 --> 00:03:50,032
on the way to the freeway and the Trade Mart.

46
00:03:50,492 --> 00:03:54,834
At about 12:30, as the car moved along Elm Street, shots were fired.

47
00:03:55,330 --> 00:03:57,614
The president and Governor Connally were both hit.

48
00:03:58,097 --> 00:04:01,675
The car raced to Parkland Memorial Hospital, a few minutes away.

49
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,102
It arrived at about twelve thirty-five.

50
00:04:04,592 --> 00:04:07,837
At about one o'clock, doctors pronounced the president dead,

51
00:04:07,887 --> 00:04:09,398
at the age of forty-six.

52
00:04:16,458 --> 00:04:18,031
Governor Connally survived.

53
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:27,930
Police sealed the Depository and found a rifle on the sixth floor,

54
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:33,372
and at about 1:16 a patrolman, J. D. Tippit, was shot dead a few miles away.

55
00:04:33,825 --> 00:04:37,670
At about 1:50, police arrested a man in the Texas Theatre:

56
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,010
Lee Harvey Oswald, aged twenty-four.

57
00:04:40,497 --> 00:04:44,776
Film from August 1963 shows him handing out leaflets in New Orleans.

58
00:04:45,258 --> 00:04:49,283
At 2:38 that afternoon, aboard Air Force One at Love Field,

59
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:51,219
Lyndon Johnson took the oath of office.

60
00:04:59,697 --> 00:05:02,524
The plane then flew to Washington with the body of the president.

61
00:05:10,997 --> 00:05:14,037
That night, Oswald was charged with the murder of the president,

62
00:05:14,087 --> 00:05:16,257
and he told reporters he had shot no one.

63
00:05:16,758 --> 00:05:21,103
On Sunday morning, 24 November, as police moved him to the county jail,

64
00:05:21,153 --> 00:05:23,354
he was shot dead on live television.

65
00:05:23,825 --> 00:05:26,977
The man who shot him was a Dallas nightclub owner named Jack Ruby.

66
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:29,647
So Oswald was never tried in a courtroom.

67
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:43,290
On Monday, 25 November, a horse-drawn caisson carried the coffin through Washington,

68
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:45,809
with leaders from many countries walking behind.

69
00:06:03,592 --> 00:06:05,877
At Arlington National Cemetery,

70
00:06:05,927 --> 00:06:10,113
Jacqueline Kennedy lit a flame at the grave, and it still burns today.

71
00:06:16,197 --> 00:06:21,597
On 29 November, President Johnson created a commission led by Chief Justice Earl Warren,

72
00:06:21,647 --> 00:06:24,701
and its report came out in September 1964.

73
00:06:25,192 --> 00:06:29,582
It concluded that three shots were fired from a sixth-floor window of the Depository.

74
00:06:30,058 --> 00:06:32,176
It concluded that Oswald acted alone.

75
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:37,389
It said it had found no evidence that Oswald or Jack Ruby was part of any conspiracy.

76
00:06:37,858 --> 00:06:39,643
One detail still divides people:

77
00:06:39,693 --> 00:06:43,018
whether a single bullet struck both Kennedy and Connally.

78
00:06:51,130 --> 00:06:54,790
The Commission itself reported some difference of opinion about that,

79
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:58,384
and Governor Connally always said he was hit by a separate shot.

80
00:06:58,863 --> 00:07:00,403
In 1979,

81
00:07:00,453 --> 00:07:05,219
a House of Representatives committee agreed that Oswald fired the shots that killed the president.

82
00:07:05,692 --> 00:07:09,077
But it also said, mainly from a police radio recording,

83
00:07:09,127 --> 00:07:10,981
that there was probably a conspiracy.

84
00:07:11,463 --> 00:07:12,823
In 1982,

85
00:07:12,873 --> 00:07:18,404
a panel of the National Academy of Sciences concluded that the recording did not support that finding.

86
00:07:18,858 --> 00:07:21,223
Polls measure belief, not proof,

87
00:07:21,273 --> 00:07:27,216
and in 2023 about two in three Americans told Gallup they believe more than one person was involved.

88
00:07:27,647 --> 00:07:32,094
The same poll found that twenty-nine percent believe Oswald acted alone.

89
00:07:32,568 --> 00:07:37,723
Since 1992, the National Archives has released millions of pages of records,

90
00:07:37,773 --> 00:07:40,546
and more as late as 2025.

91
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:42,990
They add detail about Oswald,

92
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,725
but the argument over what they prove is not finished.

93
00:07:46,225 --> 00:07:49,850
What nobody disputes is that the president was shot in Dallas,

94
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:53,009
and that the man arrested was killed before he could be tried.

95
00:07:54,053 --> 00:07:57,643
He spent less than an hour on the ground in Dallas,

96
00:07:57,693 --> 00:08:02,305
and more than sixty years later, we are still arguing about it.

